@flags
show_report version=1 id=d0000032-0032-0032-0032-000000000032

@prompt
# Task: Plant a column

The crop plotter plants seeds on a grid, one action at a time. It already knows how to fill a row; show it to fill a **column**. Comments mark the three places to touch:

1. Add PlantCol(Col) to the Action type
2. Add a setCol helper function
3. Handle PlantCol in the update function

Look at how PlantRow is implemented for guidance. PlantCol is similar but vertical.

@hint
Mirror `setRow`: map over the rows, and in each row change only the cell at the target column. `mapi` hands the callback an index; probe to see which argument it is.

@reference
### Approach (extension tasks)
1. Read the comment block: what should the new action do?
2. Find the existing feature it mirrors (`PlantRow`) and read its three parts: the Action variant, the helper, the update arm.
3. Build the column versions of each. Auto-probe is on; probe `setCol` calls to watch the grid change.
4. Unsure about `mapi`? Probe its callback and see which argument is the index.

@hints
PlantRow still works
PlantCol fills column 0
PlantCol fills column 2
row then column overlap correctly
selected seed is used for the column
Hidden copy: PlantCol fills column 0
Hidden copy: PlantCol fills column 2
Hidden copy: row then column overlap
Hidden copy: selected seed is used
Hidden copy: PlantRow still works

@code
{{include:hazel-programs/study/tasks-draft/07W-crop-plotter-extend.hz}}

@test
test
  let m = update(init, PlantCol(0)) in
  m.grove == [["🌱", "", ""], ["🌱", "", ""], ["🌱", "", ""]]
end;
test
  let m = update(init, PlantCol(2)) in
  m.grove == [["", "", "🌱"], ["", "", "🌱"], ["", "", "🌱"]]
end;
test
  let m = do(init, [PlantRow(0), PlantCol(1)]) in
  m.grove == [["🌱", "🌱", "🌱"], ["", "🌱", ""], ["", "🌱", ""]]
end;
test
  let m = do(init, [SelectSeed(2), PlantCol(1)]) in
  m.grove == [["", "🍄", ""], ["", "🍄", ""], ["", "🍄", ""]]
  && m.currentSeed == "🍄"
end;
test
  let m = update(init, PlantRow(1)) in
  m.grove == [["", "", ""], ["🌱", "🌱", "🌱"], ["", "", ""]]
end
